# Dev Server Lifecycle

The user is solely responsible for starting and stopping the DiningLens dev server.

## Do NOT (unless the user explicitly asks)

- Run `npm run dev`, `npm start`, or `node server/server.js`
- Kill, restart, or background server processes (e.g. `pkill`, `kill` on port 3000)
- Start nodemon or any long-running server in the terminal for "verification"

## Instead

- Tell the user to run `npm run dev` when they need the server running
- Use read-only checks when possible (e.g. reading code, static analysis)
- If a running server is required to verify something, ask the user to start it or confirm it is already running
